<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blue Mosque of Tabriz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1465</span> · Also known as Goy Masjid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Blue Mosque of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>, or Goy Masjid, is a mosque in Tabriz, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, completed in 1465 during the reign of the Qara Qoyunlu ruler Jahan Shah. It was famed for the blue tile mosaic that covered its walls and domes. Badly damaged by an earthquake in 1780, it lay largely in ruins until restoration in the 20th century, which preserved surviving panels of the original tilework.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blue-mosque-of-tabriz.jpg" alt="Blue Mosque of Tabriz" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saeedeh Joshaghani et al. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blue_Mosque_(Tabriz)_General_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
